 * Extract props from a TS `type FooProps = { ... }` or `interface FooProps { ... }`
 * declaration. Best-effort: handles flat fields with simple type expressions.
 *
 * When `preferredTypeName` is given (e.g. "FooterProps"), only that block's props
 * are returned if it exists — prevents sub-component internal Props types in the
 * same file from leaking into the registry row for the public component.
 * Falls back to collecting all *Props blocks when the preferred name isn't found.
 */
